{"id": "EUVD-2026-97889", "enisaUuid": "96875c25-5d7c-3a25-b021-e6b2332c4d45", "description": "Rapyd Admin from 9.0.0 before 9.20.0 contains a hard-coded credentials vulnerability that allows remote unauthenticated attackers to gain super-admin access through an AuthSeeder-created admin@laravel account with password admin. The account is seeded by the setup installer and silently re-created on every rpd:make run, letting attackers log in as a global super admin bypassing per-record authorization and tenant scoping.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T20:55:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-12T20:55:19", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/zofe/rapyd-admin/commit/acd6ee85f9e5ccec67199673b039c605d161406a", "https://github.com/zofe/rapyd-admin/releases/tag/v9.20.0", "https://github.com/zofe/rapyd-admin/blob/v9.19.0/src/Modules/Auth/Database/Seeders/AuthSeeder.php#L29-L34", "https://github.com/zofe/rapyd-admin", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rapyd-admin-9.0.0-before-9.20.0-hard-coded-super-admin-credentials-via-authseeder"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109566", "GHSA-8x56-m6rj-ff6q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5c7a476b-4201-3a38-84df-8a25a19d5e39", "product": {"name": "rapyd-admin", "vendor": {"name": "zofe"}}, "product_version": "9.0.0 <9.20.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d4b71e30-36c1-3187-b560-9ad8c0409876", "vendor": {"name": "zofe"}}], "isExploited": false}